+### Implemented open-system matrix and boundaries
+
+`open_system_benchmark` freezes **89 performance configurations and ten
+correctness controls**. For each N=1,2,4,6,8,10,12,16,20 and full/reduced basis,
+the combined-noise chain has Lindblad and MCWF at 100/500/1000 trajectories.
+Four one-atom performance controls use excited decay and driven dephasing;
+twelve two-atom full/reduced per-atom-rate controls cover decay, dephasing and
+combined noise with Lindblad/500-trajectory MCWF. One separate two-atom
+500-trajectory workload retains raw samples. Nine reduced target-size analytic
+MCWF decay controls and one raw-density coherence control are correctness only.
+This is a bounded one-axis design, not all combinations of every axis.
+
+The chain uses a=4 um, Rb=12.4 um (three-site exclusion), C6=100
+rad*um^6/us, omega=2*pi rad/us, delta=.3 rad/us, all-ground state and T=.05 us.
+The reduced N=20 dimension is D=907; this radius/geometry is distinct from the
+scaling/observable campaigns. Rates are gamma=.5/us and gamma_phi=.125/us;
+unused rates are zero. Per-atom rates multiply decay by 1+i/2 and dephasing by
+1+i/3. Decay/coherence controls use H=0 and T=2 us; the driven one-atom control
+uses omega=2*pi, delta=0 and T=2 us. Excited endpoints are used where the basis
+permits both; the reduced N=2/4 decay controls excite atom zero only. The coherence
+control starts (|g>+|r>)/sqrt(2). Tsit5 adaptive uses 1e-8/1e-10 tolerances,
+dt=None and 101 explicit times. All declarations, states, units and basis order
+are retained. The observable set is populations at distinct sites 0,N//2,N-1,
+total occupation and endpoint pair (N>1); only linear observables enter these
+ensemble comparisons.
+
+Independent NumPy/SciPy dense master equations at D<=64 use DOP853 1e-11/1e-13
+and 1e-12/1e-14 refinement with stability <=1e-9. Analytic excited decay and
+coherence exp[-(gamma+gamma_phi)t/2] inspect populations and off-diagonal density
+entries. Separate tighter SDK Lindblad histories at all 101 times check density
+error <=1e-6, trace/Hermiticity <=1e-6 and eigenvalues >=-1e-7. These raw states,
+references and eigendecompositions stay outside primary timing. Larger permitted
+Lindblad rows use tighter same-method histories; larger interacting MCWF rows
+use a saved tighter same-seed solve. Their independent interacting-reference gap
+remains explicit even when the sensitivity/statistical gates pass.
+
+Timing fixes seed20260811 and retains first + two warmups + five independent
+reset-state calls. Five separate calls at seeds20260811–20260815 measure sampling
+variability. Two-sided Hoeffding absolute bounds use alpha=1e-6 and a conservative
+union over the entire frozen matrix, observables, times and 32 call/comparison
+slots per configuration. Widths are one for site/pair and N for total occupation.
+Pooled five-seed bounds use 5*K trajectories; cross-count pooled comparisons use
+the sum of both bounds. A stochastic sensitivity reference contributes its own
+K-trajectory uncertainty. Sample standard errors are descriptive; no per-seed
+monotonic-error, relative-precision or general convergence-rate gate is asserted.
+
+Fresh Linux workers have default 1800s timeout, 4096MiB sampled RSS, Lindblad
+D<=256 and MCWF D<=1024 validation/time budgets. Preflight includes 2GiB JIT,
+D-squared histories/temporaries for Lindblad, MCWF history/workspace, sparse
+mapping/jumps and ensemble outputs. Explicit fixed seeds select EnsembleSerial;
+Julia/BLAS/OpenMP/MKL threads are one. MCWF throughput is completed trajectories
+per individual runtime, then summarized independently; completion is inferred
+from successful SDK ensemble return and manifest count, since no public progress
+counter is exposed. Raw storage has its own workload. Internal solver histories
+and ensemble outputs still allocate when raw trajectory export is disabled.
+Process-lifetime HWM includes references and writes; sampled RSS is no hard cap.
+
+`open_system_repeats.json`, `convergence.json`, `coverage.json`, real results and
+manifests, raw density/reference arrays, source/runtime hashes, worker checkpoints
+and matching JSON/CSV/Markdown companions support backend-free original/relocated
+audits. Eligible measured members alone enter type-7 runtime and throughput
+statistics. All exclusions, attempted failures and incomplete evidence persist.
+Bounded campaign acceptance accounts for excluded rows separately from successful
+coverage; full N=20 Lindblad remains open. No scientific validation, GPU, recurring
+RC or public performance approval follows.
